  "8c576eb3-e3d4-4aaf-bfdc-dbc83662fff0": {
    "id": "8c576eb3-e3d4-4aaf-bfdc-dbc83662fff0",
    "title": "Find the derivative \\[\\frac{dy}{dx}\\",
    "created_at": "2026-09-28T16:50:17.817351",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-28T16:52:40.399588",
    "messages": [
      {
        "id": "6ea0e5b6-f6fd-4add-b856-9f5693594b43",
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Find the derivative \\[\\frac{dy}{dx}\\] for the curve defined by \\(x^3 + y^3 = 6xy\\) evaluated at the point \\((3, 3)\\).",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-28T16:52:12.009414"
      },
      {
        "id": "b9c3ee19-ccda-40b6-9cf9-fcd859d9fa1a",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "To find the derivative of the curve defined by \\(x^3 + y^3 = 6xy\\) evaluated at the point \\((3, 3)\\), we need to differentiate both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\\begin{align}\n\\frac{d(x^3 + y^3)}{dx} &= x^2(3y - 6) \\\\[4pt]\n                        &= (3x)(3y - 6) \\\\[4pt]\n                        &= 9x(3y - 6)\n\\end{align}\\]\n\nTherefore, the derivative of the curve is given by:\n\n\\[\\frac{d(x^3 + y^3)}{dx} = 9x(3y - 6) \\]\n\nThe value of this derivative at the point \\((3, 3)\\) is:\n\n\\[\\frac{d(x^3 + y^3)}{dx} = 9(3)(3) - 6(3) = 18\\]\n\nSo, the derivative of the curve defined by \\(x^3 + y^3 = 6xy\\) evaluated at the point \\((3, 3)\\) is 18.",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-28T16:52:40.398745",
        "metadata": {
          "task_type": "conversation",
          "tool_used": false,
          "selected_tool": null,
          "tool_status": "Thinking...",
          "verification": null,
          "elapsed_sec": 28.39,
          "model": "TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0",
          "device": "cuda"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
